  "prompt": "Which Mailvora users came back for a second activation session on the same day? Look at the UTC days from 1 October to 31 December 2025 and count each user's session starts on each day, working the gaps out over each user's whole history. A user's first activation event starts a session, and an event more than 30 minutes after the same user's previous event starts a new one; an event exactly 30 minutes later stays in the same session. Measure each gap as the time between the two moments in event_ts, a UTC instant. When two events of a user share a moment, take them in event_name order, A to Z. Return three columns, in this order: user_id, event_day (the UTC date) and sessions, the number of sessions that started that day. Return one row for each user and day with 2 or more session starts. Any row order is fine.",
  "output_contract": {
    "columns": [
      {
        "name": "user_id",
        "type_class": "numeric"
      },
      {
        "name": "event_day",
        "type_class": "temporal"
      },
      {
        "name": "sessions",
        "type_class": "numeric"
